flickos-menu (1.21) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Power buttons: Log Out, Restart and Shut Down now take a second
    click. The first turns the button red and says to click again; it
    runs if clicked again within 4 seconds. Lock Screen still runs at
    once.
  * Quick Settings: Log Out, Restart and Shut Down next to Settings and
    Lock Screen, in every layout.
  * Grid view (Cupertino): the power buttons at the top right while
    Quick Settings, which has them, is off.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:41:06 +0800

flickos-menu (1.20) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Grid view: a click on the background closes the menu when the button
    is let go, not when it is pressed. Closing on the press left GTK
    holding the click, and from then on every click on an app only
    closed the menu.
  * Grid view: the pointer selects the app it is over, in the same blue
    as the search's first result, so one app is highlighted at a time
    and Enter starts it. The faint hover tint is gone.
  * Grid view: a click or Enter on an app that is already open brings
    its window forward (through flick-tiler 1.9's focus-app) instead of
    doing nothing. A middle click, Ctrl+click or Ctrl+Enter starts
    another copy.
  * Grid view: its background is drawn again (90% of the theme's
    background color), so icons and names stay readable over any window;
    it was fully see-through.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:26:47 +0800

